Create one relationship (edge) between two EXISTING nodes. Common
relationship types: attended, located_at, works_for, has_child,
part_of, occurred_at.

Audited: requires a non-empty `reason`; refuses missing endpoints,
self-loops, and exact-duplicate edges (same source, target,
relationship_type — use kg_delete_edge first if you mean to replace);
writes the new edge to kg_revision_log so it can be reverted. Pass
`dry_run: true` to preview without committing. Both nodes must already
exist — use kg_create_node first if needed.
